      "writtenOn": "2020-12-29T19:50:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not totally sure what you mean.\n\nThe generic goal here is to ensure that the $(out)/cryptoc/libcryptoc.a target is considered dirty/needs-updating if any source files in cryptoc have actually changed. If we never force a PHONY on $(out)/cryptoc/libcryptoc.a, the $(out)/cryptoc/libcryptoc.a file timestamp will appear to always look up-to-date. So, if a cryptoc source file changes, the EC build system will never detect it and rebuild.\n\nWe do something like this for the EC version header: https://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/master/Makefile.rules#L593,L595\n\nI\u0027m not familiar with any other way to have the correct subdir Makefile state represented in the parent Makefile. Any ideas?",
      "parentUuid": "100ac729_dc4f2f5a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "4bea8d3249fdf8c296f25758000926708eff2bb8",
